{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"auslander buchsbaum formula auslander buchsbaum formula","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","fileName":"Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Homological Algebra and Derived Functors]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Homological Algebra and Derived Functors","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"auslander buchsbaum formula auslander buchsbaum formula","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","fileName":"Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula","heading":"Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For a finitely generated module M of finite projective dimension over a Noetherian local ring R, the Auslander-Buchsbaum formula is pd_R(M) + depth(M) = depth(R).\n\nThe formula balances homological complexity against regular-sequence depth. A module requiring a longer projective resolution must have correspondingly less depth when the ambient ring remains fixed.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Homological Algebra and Derived Functors","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"auslan